  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Mazak post wrote every F word as a feed per minute, but it never wrote `G94`. A control in `G95` (from its power-on setting, an earlier program or MDI) reads `F1200` as 1200 mm per revolution.\n\nEach section preamble of `assets/posts/mazak.cps` now writes `G94` with its other modal words:\n\n```\nG17 G90 G94 G54 G40 G49 G80\n```\n\nThis is the block that the Haas post writes. #4150 (PR #4169) did the same for the Sinumerik 840D preamble. Each section restates `G94`, so a restart at a later section also gets it. The decision file `docs/decisions/4343-mazak-g94.md` records the dropped option (`G94` once in `onOpen`).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n29 Mazak goldens. Each changes in its preamble line only (`G17 G90 G5x` to `G17 G90 G94 G5x`):\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/mazak/*.nc` (17), `golden/nc/inch/mazak/*.nc` (2) and `golden/nc/synth_mazak.nc`;\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/mazak/*.nc` (7), `golden/wcs_flip/mazak_x.nc` and `golden/explain/mazak.nc`.\n\nIn `golden/explain/mazak.nc` the preamble comment now reads `(XY PLANE, ABSOLUTE POSITIONS, FEED PER MINUTE)`. The post's `commentMax` of 60 keeps whole meanings only, so \"WORK OFFSET 1\" no longer fits. The Haas explain golden ends the same way for the same block.\n\nNo other post and no toolpath changes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew suite `crates/post/tests/mazak_feed_mode.rs`:\n\n- `every_mazak_section_states_g94_before_its_first_feed`: a two-section program, metric and inch. Each section preamble is `G17 G90 G94 G54 G40 G49 G80`, and no F word comes before a `G94`.\n- `every_recorded_mazak_program_feeds_per_minute`: each recorded Mazak golden that feeds states `G94` first.\n\nBoth tests fail on `upstream/main`'s `mazak.cps` and goldens. Both pass with the fix.\n\nThe golden suites `script_mazak`, `conformance`, `program_units`, `control_comp` and `wear_comp` were rewritten with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` and pass.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate on e33fc70b9 (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 859 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 94.7 min.\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps --all-targets -p camcraft-post -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`) on e33fc70b9: 74 steps (1 build, 73 `app`), 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 47.6 min. The known fails #1950 and #2849 are red as expected.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real Mazak control.\n\n## Note for the merge order\n\nPR #4380 (#2528) adds a recorded stream `drill_full_diameter` with a new golden `recorded/golden/mazak/drill_full_diameter.nc`. That golden has the old preamble. The PR that merges second must write that golden again (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_mazak`).\n\nChangelog: Mazak post: each section preamble writes G94 (feed per minute), so a control left in G95 no longer reads the F words as feed per revolution.\n\nFixes #4343\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
